## Summary: The Contract a New Agent Must Implement

### Mandatory - the `Agent` interface (13 methods)

| Method | Signature | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `Name` | `() AgentName` | Registry key, e.g. `"claude-code"` |
| `Type` | `() AgentType` | Display name stored in metadata, e.g. `"Claude Code"` |
| `Description` | `() string` | Human-readable UI label |
| `DetectPresence` | `() (bool, error)` | Auto-detection logic |
| `GetHookConfigPath` | `() string` | Path to hook config file, empty if none |
| `SupportsHooks` | `() bool` | Whether agent has lifecycle hooks |
| `ParseHookInput` | `(hookType HookType, reader io.Reader) (*HookInput, error)` | Parse stdin from hook callbacks |
| `GetSessionID` | `(input *HookInput) string` | Extract session ID from hook input |
| `ProtectedDirs` | `() []string` | Dirs never touched by rewind (e.g. `[".claude"]`) |
| `GetSessionDir` | `(repoPath string) (string, error)` | Where agent stores sessions |
| `ResolveSessionFile` | `(sessionDir, agentSessionID string) string` | Transcript file path for a session |
| `ReadSession` | `(input *HookInput) (*AgentSession, error)` | Read session in native format |
| `WriteSession` | `(session *AgentSession) error` | Write session for resumption |
| `FormatResumeCommand` | `(sessionID string) string` | CLI command to resume a session |

### Optional interfaces (capability upgrades via interface composition)

| Interface | Extra Methods | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `HookSupport` | `InstallHooks`, `UninstallHooks`, `AreHooksInstalled`, `GetSupportedHooks` | Full hook lifecycle management |
| `HookHandler` | `GetHookNames() []string` | Custom hook verb vocabulary for `entire hooks <agent>` subcommands |
| `FileWatcher` | `GetWatchPaths`, `OnFileChange` | For agents without hooks (e.g. Aider) |
| `TranscriptAnalyzer` | `GetTranscriptPosition`, `ExtractModifiedFilesFromOffset` | Efficient checkpoint diffing |
| `TranscriptChunker` | `ChunkTranscript`, `ReassembleTranscript` | Splitting transcripts past GitHub's 100MB limit |

### Registration pattern

Each agent self-registers via `init()`:
```go
func init() {
    agent.Register(agent.AgentNameClaudeCode, func() agent.Agent {
        return &ClaudeCodeAgent{}
    })
}
```

The `Factory` type is `func() Agent` - a zero-argument constructor returning the `Agent` interface. The registry is protected by `sync.RWMutex` and supports auto-detection via `Detect()` which iterates all factories calling `DetectPresence()`.

